 on the heels of the new  brad wright stargate series that would  you know work together with that this  news was dropped by giant freaking robot  something like a year after that and  that story became popular it was widely  dismissed as being nonsense but i am  told at the end of 2019 that was the  plan around this time  late 2019 into early 2020 there were  several rewrites of the script now brad  wright has talked about this himself how  there was a normal development process  he would basically send his work back  into mgm they would do little notes on  it and send it back and he would work on  it until he figured out a script that  worked for everybody  now i am actually told that amazon were  already involved in this project even  then that they were planning to be the  customer that basically mgm would put  stargate on amazon prime now that makes  complete sense because amazon prime and  mgm already had a reasonably close  working relationship at that point  amazon does have an mgm channel on it so  even then amazon prime were feeding  there  so even then amazon prime were feeding  back through mgm to brad and trying to  get him to go in a certain direction at  this point covid really hit us in the  backside and the entire planet basically  stopped for 12 months and so did  development of stargate franchise  nothing then happened for about 12  months oh by the way if you do like the  content please consider hitting the join  button and becoming a fully fledged side  tracker you can also go to side  dashtrack.com and pick marvelous  merchandise all these little things  really help the channel also if you're  new to the channel like subscribe hit  that bell notification and share the  video wherever the hell you want  but then in march 2021 something very  interesting did happen  steve wright became the new executive  producer in charge of scripted material  at mgm he then immediately scrapped the  idea of an animated series to go along  with brad rights he said  we don't have the resources to do that  and we wouldn't do a very good job the  mgm animation studio is crap it was  actually scrapped not long after i am  also told that this is around the first  time that real serious doubts about brad  wright's script began to surface  it was around this time that amazon did  more loudly start voicing its concerns  about what it was seeing and even some  people at mgm started to doubt that this  project of brads would have any real  weight moving forwards was it just a  coincidence that steve wright took his  position as the head and president of  mgm at the same time or was actually  steve wright that was voicing these  concerns most loudly in may 2021 amazon  bought mgm for 8.5 billion dollars now  they were not the only people interested  and actually in the run-up before this  apple were the most interested in buying  mgm at this time mgm was being told by  amazon that they were going to be  allowed to have free reign moving  forwards that they should start working  on some new projects and amazon planned  to give them full creative control and  amazon would only really act as a  customer that they wouldn't just come in  and slash everybody's jobs and take over  mgm was really convinced that they were  going to have full creative control so  it was around this time that mgm started  working on a second script for a new  stargaze show now we've never really  been able to quite figure out where this  script came from but talking to a lot of  different people i suspect and this is  only my opinion but i suspect this was  actually a dean devlin script that was  written back in 2017  now i don't think the intention was ever  to actually make this script happen i  think it was a  idea that they would sort of contrast  and compare the two scripts and the two  different visions for how stargate could  move forwards it was something that they  would then show to amazon later on and  that they would get a bit of an idea of  hopefully what everybody wanted to do  moving forwards  but they did continue to develop both  scripts doing initial artworks lots of  initial storyboarding they really  started to put me on the bones of the  existing scripts and really started to  get an idea of what the vision for both  would be so in march 2022  everything changed  the sale of mgm to amazon was finalized  and amazon to be fair  dropped the hammer michael deluca and  pamela abdi resigned in april of 2022  resigned over pushed is the big question  but they've never really spoken about  why they resigned that is because they  almost certainly contracted not to and  they would have almost certainly had to  sign some sort of contract when they got  their enormous payouts when they left  what i am told is though that they left  because it became very evident to mgm  that everything they'd been told in the  run-up to this point was a complete lie  that they were not going to be given  creative control that they were not  going to be allowed to continue to  operate as mgm and actually amazon were  coming in and they were taking over  everything and that even amazon  executives at this point said that mgm  would be absorbed into amazon pictures  they started using excuses like covid to  explain why these changes were happening  and why they were forced to take over  mgm rather than just allow it to carry  on operating as one of the biggest  studios of in history and then amazon  put all of mgm's projects into a kind of  stalling process  anything that wasn't in pre-production  was just frozen they all went into  review and small teams throughout amazon  studios began reviewing everything they  were looking at amazon were not at all  impressed with what they found now even  though mgm was being operated reasonably  well as a business it actually had been  profitable for a few years  creatively amazon were just  furious by what they found when they  started looking into it they found  ridiculous projects in development lots  of infighting apparently between  directors and producers etc and just a  complete mess  stargate was always intended to be one  of the big announcements they wanted to  pull off straight away there was always  going to be three big things that amazon  wanted to do as soon as they took over  mgm bond and that's been completely  screwed up stargate  and something from the intellectual  properties  some big new reboot or remake  none of those things have happened  simply because of what i'm telling you  that mgm was in such a bad way and  amazon had such a big job of absorbing  it into amazon prime that they just  simply couldn't allow them to continue  with any of the projects they had  planned  we actually did come  this close to brad wright's script  getting greenlit  mgm was planning to do it the second the  sale went through the second amazon gave  them the final go ahead mgm were gonna  push forward  i kept hearing rumors that brad wright's  script was not dead and buried and that  it was still possible  however becoming more and more unlikely  that it could still get made and again i  came on my channel and told you that  brad wright's project  was not going to happen this was only  then really confirmed by brad wright on  july 27th in a live video stream where  he actually said again that he never  thought his script was ever going to see  the light of day  so the voices that started a year and a  half ago  doubting brad wright's project did just  get louder and louder  but that is not the end of the story for  stargate because they are trying to  figure something out with this they are  trying to develop a new series but they  don't just want to create a series they  want to create a franchise because all  of the studios want everything to become  a franchise nowadays that's just the way  [ __ ] works nowadays  so as i told you a few weeks ago mark  ferguson hawk ostby the guys that um  created the expanse for amazon have been  approached to develop something for  stargate they're not necessarily being  asked to write a script for what i'm  being told instead they're being asked  to develop an outline of what the new  series would look like and how it could  form the part of a franchise for a new  series of series now from what i've been  told they're not actually being asked to  write a script or a pilot for stargate  instead they're being asked to develop  something a universe that fits with  canon for what we've already seen of  stargate sg1 sg and sga  but something that makes sense in a  larger picture so what they're really  being asked to do is create sort of like  a stargate bible this is something they  used to do for star trek all time star  trek the next generation famously had a  bible that gene roddenberry put together  it was something they dipped in and out  of throughout the seven seasons that is  what  hawke and mark are being asked to  produce now now that might lead into  them writing a pilot but at the moment  instead they're just trying to really  figure out how the hell they move  forward to stargate now on that point me  and matt this week are going to be doing  a couple of videos on how stargate could  come back whether it be a hard reboot or  a continuation of the story what are  fans going to be really excited about  and what are the challenges that maybe  might turn fans off  so look forward to those tuesday and  thursday this week on sidetrek  so don't forget guys that if you enjoy  the content please consider hitting the  join button and becoming a fully fledged  side tracker also if you are new to the  channel please like subscribe hit that  bell notification it really helps us out  and as always guys uh please stay safe  i'll see you next time  [Music]  you
 

